A||N||5||Ditz88GT||Bad water pump?||||5||
Z||000000||Ditz88GT||06-08-2000||01:17 AM||||How can I tell if I have a bad water pump? It's not dripping, but it's the only thing left I can think of to stop the overheating. I replaced the head gasket, rad cap, thermo housing cap, thermostat & and I got all the air out of the system.  When the car is running I can't feel pressure through the hose by squeezing  it. I opened the rad cap and the coolant appears to move, but not really fast. Does this sound like a bad water pump?  Any help on this would be great!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Ditz88GT (edited 06-08-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||06-08-2000||01:34 AM||||well it could be the impeller on the pump. some have a plastic one that will slip. but it could be the radiator. I had to replace mine. it was plugged and I couldnt tell until it was removed. got a lifetime one fopr $80.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ditz88GT||06-08-2000||09:44 AM||||WOW, 80 bucks! Where did you find a radiator for that price?  The cheapest I could find was $175.00.  I think I'm replacing the water pump and the radiator anyway.  Even if it is not a fix I know it won't hurt.  Thanks for your help Tom.||||reg||3
Z||000003||87PegasusGT||06-08-2000||06:12 PM||||My water pump and head gasket were gone when I had the problem you are describing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jlruiz67||06-11-2000||06:38 PM||||Well that sounds so familiar, My 87 Gt ran like a champ and out of the blue I started to get really hot on stop lights and cooler once I got going. Untill it pegd on the red and I stoped the car really fast and towed it to my local PepBoys. what do you know, it was the water Pump after all. Now I'm back in the game and ready for the rest of the upgrades I want to do. I water pump is a terrible thing to waste. hehehe.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||06-11-2000||09:56 PM||||Instead of replacing the radiator, take it to a shop and have it "rodded-out."  They basically shove metal rods through the coolant passages to clean blockages... It made my old Z28 like a new car.  No more overheating... Problem was that the previous owner got nuts with the sealant when changing a water pump.  It only cost about 25 bucks.||||reg||1
